  "title": "John D NDE 6417",
  "date": "1965",
  "content": "I was shot and fell by the roots of a tree. As I lay there, all grew quiet. I heard songbirds singing in the branches above me. I wondered where they came from because a battle usually ran off all wild life. I was at great peace and in no pain. Suddenly and without warning, my stomach had a cramp and I felt and heard a breath tearing into my lungs, which began to burn now. I looked down and could see my small intestines coming out of a hole in me. I quickly looked away again as this information was disturbing. I could not move after a while, not even move my eyes or close them. I heard a voice say ‘hey this one is still pumping out blood, is he alive then?’ Someone else pulled me on a stretcher and was running. I went into a dream; saw all but did not let it affect me I was at peace. I saw myself being put on a table and people were doing things to my body. I still was an observer only at this point. I heard someone say, ‘we are losing him’, and someone else said, ‘give him 2 cc of (something). Suddenly BANG, I was back in my pain-wrecked body again. I spoke, the surgeon said. ‘Be quiet we are fixing you. Go back to sleep.’ I took him at his word and fell asleep, waking a week later in Japan in one of the famous buildings there for the Vietnam wounded.",
